From 5f2e5a8a9d8ebce71a5cffed5d01f5b5a662383b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Basanagouda Nagappa Koppad <basanagouda.nagappa.koppad@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:43:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] graphic: Add hwc.info service (libhwcservice) for HDCP

Intel hwc.info vndbinder service used by Intel HDCP clients, moved
here from the drm_hwcomposer adaptation patch: it is hand-written
binder code (hwc.IService, hwc.IControls, hwc.IDiagnostic), which
Soong allows only under vendor/ and hardware/. Module names and
install paths are unchanged:

 - graphic/hwcservice/libhwcservice: client/server interface library
   (from the Intel drm-hwcomposer fork, commits 56c1a5b, 5167ccd).
 - graphic/hwcservice/libhwcservice/test: hwcservice_test.
 - graphic/hwcservice/service: libhwcservicelib, dlopen()ed by
   android.hardware.composer.hwc3-service.drm. It talks to the HWC
   through the C ops table in hwcservice_ops.h
   (libhwcservice_ops_headers, from the external/drm_hwcomposer Intel
   patch "Add hwc.info service (libhwcservice) for HDCP").

Changes compared with the fork:
 - The requested HDCP content type is passed to the HWC.
   HWCS_CP_CONTENT_TYPE1 (HDCP 2.2 or newer) no longer falls back to
   HDCP 1.4; unknown content types are rejected with BAD_VALUE.
 - Client proxies return the binder transaction error instead of
   reading the empty reply (which reported failed disable and SRM
   calls as success), and DumpOptions() writes the interface token the
   service checks.
 - SetHDCPSRM*() return INVALID_OPERATION: SRM programming is not
   implemented, and the fork reported the discarded revocation list as
   applied (OK).
 - hwcservice_test: one action per run with explicit operands
   (-h <connector> <type>, -i <connector>, -j <type>, -k), validated
   before connecting; the fork read argv[0] without checking it and
   derived the content type from the display number. Unused locals
   from the fork's removed mode/color options are gone.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1589
Signed-off-by: Basanagouda Nagappa Koppad <basanagouda.nagappa.koppad@intel.com>
